---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Goldfish: sign and forget" caveat description="Goldfish is a Bitcoin signer you build from an off-the-shelf board and a printed case. Load your seed from a QR code, sign, unplug. Nothing is saved.">
<style is:global>
  /* Page-only styles. Screens are the real ones from firmware/docs/screens, inside devices drawn in CSS. */
  h2 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 38px); letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.12; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); max-width: 52ch; margin-top: 10px; }

  /* ---- a device: printed case, black glass, the firmware's screen */
  /* The case has its glass on top, edge to edge: from the front you see black glass,
     and the printed case only as its side below it, with the USB-C port. */
  .device {
    --w: 240px;
    width: calc(var(--w) * 1.14);   /* --w is the screen's width: 240px shows the 240x320 screenshot pixel for pixel */
    padding-bottom: calc(var(--w) * .05);
    position: relative; flex: none;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 calc(var(--w) * .08) calc(var(--w) * .07) rgba(20, 34, 43, .25));
  }
  .device .glass {
    position: relative; z-index: 1; background: #0B0E10;
    border-radius: calc(var(--w) * .09); padding: calc(var(--w) * .1) calc(var(--w) * .07) calc(var(--w) * .16);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, .08);
  }
  .device img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; border-radius: calc(var(--w) * .02); background: var(--paper); display: block; }
  .device::before {              /* the case under the glass: the same rounded shape, shifted down */
    content: ""; position: absolute; inset: calc(var(--w) * .05) 0 0 0;
    border-radius: calc(var(--w) * .09); background: var(--case);
    box-shadow: inset 0 calc(var(--w) * -.008) 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .12);
  }
  .device::after {               /* USB-C socket in the case's side */
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: calc(var(--w) * .014); translate: -50% 0;
    width: calc(var(--w) * .17); height: calc(var(--w) * .032); border-radius: 99px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .5);
  }

  /* hero: the device with hand-drawn notes around it */
  .hero-fig { position: relative; width: 760px; max-width: 100%; margin: 0 auto 44px; }
  .hero-fig > .device { margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero-fig .notes { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 0; translate: -50% 0; width: 760px; height: 440px; pointer-events: none; overflow: visible; }
  .notes path { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .notes text { font: 700 23px Caveat, "Segoe Print", "Comic Sans MS", cursive; fill: var(--accent); }
  .notes-list { display: none; }

  /* ---- hero */
  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 24px 0 96px; }
  .hero-fig { padding-bottom: 46px; }
  .hero-fig .device img { animation: boot .9s ease-out .15s both; }   /* plugged in: the screen comes on, once */
  @keyframes boot { from { opacity: 0; } }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(42px, 7.6vw, 72px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.02; max-width: 12ch; margin: 0 auto; }
  .hero .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(17px, 2.2vw, 20px); margin: 20px auto 0; max-width: 34ch; }
  .hero .cta { margin-top: 32px; }
  .more { display: flex; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 22px; margin-top: 18px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
  .more a { text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-color: var(--line); }
  .more a:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .status {
    display: inline-flex; gap: 10px; align-items: baseline; text-align: left; margin-top: 44px; padding: 10px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .status b {                  /* the firmware's TESTNET tag */
    background: var(--amber-dim); color: var(--amber); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 6px; white-space: nowrap;
  }

  section { padding: 88px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }

  /* ---- the signing walk-through */
  .demo { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 64px; align-items: center; margin-top: 40px; }
  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: step; }
  .steps button {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; column-gap: 14px; width: 100%; text-align: left;
    padding: 14px 16px; border: 0; border-radius: 14px; background: none; color: var(--faint); font: inherit; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .steps button::before {
    counter-increment: step; content: counter(step); grid-row: span 2; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; background: var(--raised); color: var(--muted);
  }
  .steps button strong { font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); }
  .steps button span { grid-column: 2; font-size: 15px; display: none; max-width: 40ch; }
  .steps button:hover strong { color: var(--text); }
  .steps button[aria-current=step] { background: var(--raised); }
  .steps button[aria-current=step]::before { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  .steps button[aria-current=step] strong { color: var(--text); }
  .steps button[aria-current=step] span { display: block; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }
  .stage { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; width: 330px; }
  .stage .device { --w: 240px; cursor: pointer; border: 0; font: inherit; display: block; background: none; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; }
  .stage .device img { transition: opacity .25s; }
  .stage.off .device img { opacity: 0; }
  /* plugged in, the plug's tip sits in the socket (so the socket itself is hidden);
     unplugged, the cable drops away and the empty socket shows */
  .cable { width: 46px; height: 120px; margin-top: -12px; position: relative; z-index: 2; transition: translate .5s cubic-bezier(.3, 0, .2, 1), opacity .5s; }
  .stage .device::after { opacity: 0; transition: opacity .3s; }
  .stage.off .device::after { opacity: 1; }
  .stage.off .cable { translate: 0 46px; opacity: .45; }
  .hint { color: var(--faint); font-size: 14px; margin-top: 4px; min-height: 1.5em; }
  .tryit { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 40px; }
  .tryit a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* ---- three facts */
  .facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 40px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .facts svg { width: 44px; height: 44px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .facts p { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 6px; font-size: 16px; }

  /* ---- text beside a picture */
  .split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
  .trio { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-end; gap: 12px; }
  /* Screens at 2/3 size and never rotated: a rotation resamples every pixel and blurs the
     small UI text. The three overlap a little so they still fit half the page. */
  .trio .device { --w: 160px; }
  .trio .device + .device { margin-left: -44px; }
  .trio .device:nth-child(1) { --case: var(--graphite); }
  .trio .device:nth-child(2) { translate: 0 -24px; z-index: 1; }
  .trio .device:nth-child(3) { --case: var(--white); }
  .photo { border-radius: 20px; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; object-fit: cover; }
  .ways { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 24px 0 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .ways li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 10px 1fr; gap: 14px; align-items: baseline; color: var(--muted); }
  .ways li::before { content: ""; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--accent); }
  .ways b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

  .also { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 32px 40px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .also p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 16px; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* ---- build */
  .build { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .build a {
    display: block; padding: 22px; border-radius: 16px; background: var(--raised); text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent; transition: border-color .15s;
  }
  .build a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .build i { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: #fff; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .build p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .build + .photo { margin-top: 16px; aspect-ratio: 16 / 7; object-position: 50% 42%; }


  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .hero-fig .notes { display: none; }
    .notes-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 4px 16px; margin: 16px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none;
      font: 700 21px Caveat, "Segoe Print", cursive; color: var(--accent); }
    .hero { padding: 32px 0 72px; }
    section { padding: 64px 0; }
    .demo, .split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .stage { margin: 0 auto; order: -1; }   /* device above the steps, so a tap on a step shows */
    .facts, .also, .build { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .build { gap: 12px; }
    .trio .device { --w: 112px; }
    .trio .device + .device { margin-left: -30px; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hero-fig .device img { animation: none; }
    .cable, .stage .device img { transition: none; }
  }
</style>

<main>
  <div class="wrap hero">
    <figure class="hero-fig">
      <div class="device"><div class="glass"><img src="img/screens/1_home.png" alt="The home screen: goldfish, Sign and forget, with Enter words and Scan QR"></div></div>
      <svg class="notes" viewBox="0 0 760 440" aria-hidden="true">
        <defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="11" markerHeight="11" markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" orient="auto"><path d="M1 1 L8.5 5 L1 9"/></marker></defs>
        <text x="44" y="78">2″ touch screen</text>
        <path d="M120 92 C 150 120, 205 112, 252 130" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
        <text x="20" y="262">no Wi-Fi, no Bluetooth</text>
        <path d="M150 274 C 185 290, 212 262, 236 240" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
        <text x="560" y="88">camera on the back</text>
        <path d="M612 100 C 602 140, 570 156, 526 160" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
        <text x="550" y="254">your seed lives in</text>
        <text x="550" y="278">memory only</text>
        <path d="M562 292 C 548 318, 530 312, 506 300" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
        <text x="440" y="432">power via USB</text>
        <path d="M436 424 C 412 422, 398 414, 392 400" marker-end="url(#ah)"/>
      </svg>
      <figcaption><ul class="notes-list"><li>2″ touch screen</li><li>no Wi-Fi, no Bluetooth</li><li>camera on the back</li><li>your seed lives in memory only</li><li>power via USB</li></ul></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <h1>Sign and forget.</h1>
    <p class="sub">Goldfish is a Bitcoin signer that forgets. Scan your seed, sign, unplug. Nothing is saved, so there is nothing left to find.</p>
    <a class="cta" href="#build">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
      Build one yourself
    </a>
    <div class="more">
      <a href="#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="try/">Try it in your browser</a>
      <a href="flasher/">Flash the firmware</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/reneaaron/goldfish">Source on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <div><p class="status"><b>Early days</b><span>It works in the desktop simulator and has not been tested on real hardware yet. Don't use it for real funds.</span></p></div>
  </div>

  <section id="how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Sign a transaction, then pull the plug</h2>
      <p class="lede">Everything goes in through the camera and out through the screen. Tap through it.</p>
      <div class="demo">
        <ol class="steps" id="steps">
          <li><button data-shot="2_scan_waiting"><strong>Scan your seed</strong><span>Hold your SeedQR up to the camera. Or type your words.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot="3_seed_loaded"><strong>Match the fingerprint</strong><span>The device shows which seed it loaded, so you can check it against your wallet app.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot="7_psbt_overview"><strong>Scan the transaction</strong><span>Your wallet app shows it as a QR. The device reads the amount, the fee and the change.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot="8_psbt_output_1"><strong>Check every address</strong><span>One screen per recipient. Change only counts as change if your seed really owns it.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot="10_psbt_sign"><strong>Slide to sign</strong><span>The device only signs. Your wallet app sends.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot="11_psbt_signed"><strong>Scan it back</strong><span>The signed transaction comes out as a QR for your wallet app.</span></button></li>
          <li><button data-shot=""><strong>Unplug</strong><span>The seed was only in memory. Now it's gone.</span></button></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="stage" id="stage">
          <button class="device" id="demo-device" aria-label="Next step">
            <div class="glass"><img id="shot" src="img/screens/2_scan_waiting.png" alt="The device's screen at this step"></div>
          </button>
          <svg class="cable" viewBox="0 0 46 120" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="11" y="0" width="24" height="10" rx="2.5" fill="#9AA3A8"/>
            <rect x="6" y="8" width="34" height="34" rx="8" fill="#2B3338"/>
            <path d="M23 42v78" stroke="#2B3338" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
          <p class="hint" id="hint">Tap the device for the next step</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="tryit">Those were screenshots. <a href="try/">Run the real firmware in your browser →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Less to trust</h2>
      <div class="facts">
        <div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="9" width="30" height="26" rx="6" fill="#FF7A2F"/><path d="M15 9V5m7 4V5m7 4V5M15 39v-4m7 4v-4m7 4v-4" stroke="#FF7A2F" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M17 18l10 8m0-8l-10 8" stroke="#14222B" stroke-width="3"/></svg>
          <h3>Nothing is saved</h3>
          <p>The seed lives in memory only. The firmware never writes to storage, so an unplugged device holds nothing.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 18a23 23 0 0 1 32 0M12 25a14.5 14.5 0 0 1 20 0" stroke="#FF7A2F" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="22" cy="33" r="3.5" fill="#FF7A2F"/><path d="M7 39L37 6" stroke="#14222B" stroke-width="4"/></svg>
          <h3>No radio, no USB data</h3>
          <p>The board has no Wi-Fi or Bluetooth hardware, and the firmware has no USB stack: the cable only powers it. Use a charger or a power bank. (Update firmware is the one exception: you choose it, and the board restarts as a USB drive.)</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="#FF7A2F"><rect x="5" y="5" width="14" height="14" rx="3"/><rect x="25" y="5" width="14" height="14" rx="3"/><rect x="5" y="25" width="14" height="14" rx="3"/><rect x="25" y="25" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/><rect x="33" y="33" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/></g><g fill="#14222B"><rect x="9.5" y="9.5" width="5" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="29.5" y="9.5" width="5" height="5" rx="1"/><rect x="9.5" y="29.5" width="5" height="5" rx="1"/></g></svg>
          <h3>QR codes in, QR codes out</h3>
          <p>Seeds, transactions and addresses come in through the camera. Signatures leave on the screen.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>You are the random number generator</h2>
        <p class="lede">The firmware has none. A new seed is made only from what you put in.</p>
        <ul class="ways">
          <li><span><b>Roll a die</b> 50 times for 12 words.</span></li>
          <li><span><b>Flip a coin</b> 128 times.</span></li>
          <li><span><b>Draw 11 words</b> yourself. The last one comes from coin flips.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="trio">
        <div class="device"><div class="glass"><img src="img/screens/16_dice.png" alt="Dice rolls screen: 23 of 50 rolls entered"></div></div>
        <div class="device"><div class="glass"><img src="img/screens/24_coins.png" alt="Coin flips screen: 37 of 128 flips entered"></div></div>
        <div class="device"><div class="glass"><img src="img/screens/15_new_seed.png" alt="New seed screen: dice rolls, coin flips or draw words"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap split">
      <img class="photo" src="img/renders/13_backup_copy.png" alt="Render: a signer next to a paper card with a seed QR being filled in" loading="lazy">
      <div>
        <h2>Back it up with a pen</h2>
        <p class="lede">Write down the words, or copy the seed onto a paper QR card. The device shows the grid part by part, then scans your card to check you got every square right.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Also in there</h2>
      <div class="also">
        <div><h3>Verify an address</h3><p>Scan a receive address to confirm it belongs to your seed before you share it.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Multisig</h3><p>Scan your wallet's descriptor, check it on the device, then sign as one of the cosigners.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Child seeds</h3><p>Derive a BIP-85 child seed and back it up like a new one.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Passphrase</h3><p>Add a BIP-39 passphrase. Only the derived key is kept, and only until you unplug.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Connect a wallet</h3><p>Show your xpub as a QR so a wallet app can watch your balance and build transactions.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Native segwit only</h3><p>Single-sig and sorted multisig, on mainnet and testnet.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="build">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Build one</h2>
      <p class="lede">One off-the-shelf board with a touch screen, one camera, one printed case that clips shut. No soldering iron in the parts list.</p>
      <div class="build">
        <a href="build/#parts"><i>1</i><h3>Get the parts</h3><p>A Waveshare RP2350-Touch-LCD-2 and an OV5640 camera.</p></a>
        <a href="build/#print"><i>2</i><h3>Print the case</h3><p>STL and STEP files, in whatever colour you like.</p></a>
        <a href="build/#flash"><i>3</i><h3>Flash the firmware</h3><p>From your browser: hold BOOT, plug in, pick the drive.</p></a>
      </div>
      <img class="photo" src="img/renders/06_lineup.png" alt="Render: four signers in graphite, white and orange cases showing different screens" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script is:inline>
const buttons = [...document.querySelectorAll('#steps button')];
const stage = document.getElementById('stage');
const shot = document.getElementById('shot');
const hint = document.getElementById('hint');
let at = 0;

function show(i) {
  at = i;
  buttons.forEach((b, n) => n === i ? b.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step') : b.removeAttribute('aria-current'));
  const name = buttons[i].dataset.shot;
  stage.classList.toggle('off', !name);
  if (name) shot.src = 'img/screens/' + name + '.png';
  hint.textContent = name ? 'Tap the device for the next step' : 'Tap to plug it back in';
}

buttons.forEach((b, i) => b.addEventListener('click', () => show(i)));
document.getElementById('demo-device').addEventListener('click', () => show((at + 1) % buttons.length));
buttons.forEach((b) => { if (b.dataset.shot) new Image().src = 'img/screens/' + b.dataset.shot + '.png'; });
show(0);
</script>
</Base>
